       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (immediate-release, FDA labeling). It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nI suspect one of these was intended:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This totals 2,550 mg/day, which is the maximum.\n- **1700 mg/day in divided doses.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** These are common regimens.\n\nWhich dose and frequency do you want? If 1700 mg three times daily is intentional, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note documenting the confirmation."
